For your college-ai-assistant project specifically

I would check it in this order:

Phase 1 — AI Quality
Test 20–50 college-related questions.
Check correct vs incorrect answers.
Check hallucinations.
Check whether answers are grounded in your college data.
Test unclear and unexpected questions.
Phase 2 — Application
Add proper error handling.
Check API key security.
Test response time.
Test multiple requests.
Check Cloud Run reliability.
Phase 3 — Business
Estimate cost per query.
Estimate monthly cost.
Improve chatbot user experience.
Phase 4 — Production
Add logging.
Add monitoring.
Add 👍 / 👎 feedback.
Use GitHub versioning.
Re-evaluate after every important update.

So yes — if you want to work professionally, don't stop at “my AI app is deployed.” The next level is to measure, test, monitor, secure, and continuously improve it.

Your mam has essentially given you a Production Readiness Checklist. We can now apply this checklist step by step to your existing college-ai-assistant project, starting with AI/RAG Quality testing, then moving to security, logging, monitoring, cost, and feedback.

A production-ready college AI assistant needs measurable quality checks, so the first concrete step is 
creating a 20-question evaluation set for your college data and scoring answer accuracy, grounding, and hallucinations before adding more infrastructure.

